# Git LFS — track large generated figure artifacts.
#
# Research figures are the class of file that measurably bloats the repo
# (~16.8 MB across 36 files at the time of the PR #11 NLA arc). The
# 2026-05-31 history rewrite ran `git lfs migrate import` to move all
# existing figure blobs into LFS (see the `project-repo-lfs-rewrite` note);
# this rule keeps figures added afterward in LFS too. Run `git lfs install`
# before working the repo, or figures show as phantom modifications.
#
# Scoped to figure directories anywhere under `research/` — every arc
# (`research/arcs/<slug>/observations/figures/`) plus the one-off
# `research/observations/figures/` bin. That is currently every PNG the repo
# tracks; the narrow scope is deliberate, so a small incidental PNG added
# elsewhere later stays a regular git object rather than silently entering LFS.
research/**/figures/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Git LFS — track raw research datasets (the `.pt` capture/derived artifacts
# a figure or audit is generated from). Committing these alongside the
# figures and scripts is what makes an arc reproducible from a clean clone:
# without them, the figure-render scripts and the four
# `<family>_audit_findings.py` scripts (nla / subliminal / emb / jspace)
# have no input to load. They are tensor dumps (a few KB to ~180 MB each;
# ~15 MB in arc 01, ~96 MB in arc 03, ~272 MB in arc 04 not counting the
# cache/ tree covered by the next rule), so LFS is the right home — same
# rationale as the figures rule above. Scoped to
# a `data/` directory anywhere under `research/` (every arc's
# `research/arcs/<slug>/data/`, plus a future one-off
# `research/observations/data/`). See `research/ARC_PROCESS.md`
# § "Raw data is a deliverable".
research/**/data/*.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Git LFS — the arc-04 committed lens cache (see the .gitignore arc-04
# exception): full fitted lens tensors are 120-662 MiB each, far past the
# point where LFS is optional. The data/*.pt rule above does not reach into
# cache/ (its glob requires the file directly inside a data/ directory).
research/**/data/cache/*.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Git LFS — track archived primary-source PDFs. Paper snapshots (print-to-PDF
# of HTML publications, arxiv PDFs) run 1–15 MB each; same bloat rationale as
# the figures rule. First population: gurnee2026-workspace (2026-07-18).
theory/sources/papers/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
